@startuml SequenceAddTask
title Week 4 - Add a task
actor User
participant "Input / Add Task button" as UI
participant "main.js" as Main
participant TodoController as Controller
participant TodoService as Service
participant LocalStorageHandler as Storage
participant "Browser localStorage" as BrowserStorage
participant TodoRenderer as Renderer
participant "Task container / document" as Page

User -> UI : Enter description and click Add Task
UI -> Main : click handler
Main -> Controller : addTask(input.value, 'simple')
Controller -> Service : addTask(description, type)
Service -> Service : Trim and validate description

alt Description has fewer than 3 characters
  Service -> User : alert validation message
  Service --> Controller : null
  Controller --> Main : null
  note over Main, Page : Input and rendered lists remain unchanged
else Valid description
  Service -> Service : Create task and append to tasks
  note right of Service
    Warn if the existing list has at least 20 tasks.
    For Add Urgent, type is 'urgent':
    set high priority and prefix the description.
  end note
  Service -> Storage : save(tasks)
  Storage -> BrowserStorage : setItem('todo-tasks', JSON.stringify(tasks))
  Service --> Controller : task.id
  Controller -> Renderer : render(service, task.id)
  Renderer -> Service : getWorkloadSummary()
  Service --> Renderer : workload text
  Renderer -> Renderer : Read service.tasks and build both lists
  Renderer -> Page : Update lists, status, and page title
  Renderer -> Page : Bind actions and flash the new row
  Controller --> Main : task.id
  Main -> UI : Clear input
end

note over UI, Main : Enter triggers Add Task; Add Urgent uses the same flow with type 'urgent'.
@enduml
